[PAUSE 3 SECONDS]

If a temperature value is noisy or implausible, compare the installed sensor type with the configured input type. Then check drawings, terminations, and approved diagnostics. Do not assume a sensor is defective just because the display is wrong; configuration and wiring can create similar symptoms.

[PAUSE 3 SECONDS]

For this lesson, remember the core distinction: RTD means changing resistance; thermocouple means a small voltage related to temperature difference. Use the manufacturer’s documentation for sensor curves, wire colors, and terminal details.', '2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z') on conflict (lesson_id, version) do update set script = excluded.script;
